00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.926
After you complete
this lab on Quiklabs,

00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:10.735
you'll finally
unlock your badge.

00:00:10.735 --> 00:00:12.360
On this episode,
we're going to go over

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.000
what you'll learn in this
final lab, Google Genomics Quik

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.840
Start.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.970
Google Genomics helps the
life science community

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.010
organize the world's
genomic information

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.170
and make it
accessible and useful.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.500
Big genomic data is here today
with petabytes rapidly growing

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.860
towards exabytes.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.370
Google Genomics is an API that
is part of the Google Cloud

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.540
Platform.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.040
Through this and
other add-ons, you

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.410
can apply the same technologies
that power Google Search

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.050
and Maps to securely store,
process, explore, and share

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.460
large, complex data sets.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.560
In this lab, you'll use
Google's implementation

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.400
of the htsget protocol and
SAMtools to create a project

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.350
and view some public
data for yourself.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.660
To access genomic data stored
in Google Cloud Storage,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.118
you can use Google's
implementation

00:00:53.118 --> 00:00:55.920
of the htsget protocol,
defined by the Global Alliance

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.970
for Genomics and Health.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.060
Google's htsget
implementation makes

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.880
it easy to access and share
data stored in your own cloud

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.850
projects without copying large
files to and from Compute

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.920
Engine virtual machines.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.560
You can also use the htsget
server to access data

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.810
from public sources, like
Google's mirror of the 1,000

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.310
Genomes Project.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:14.880
Is this it?

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.350
Is this the last
lab on your quest?

